<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar cane crushing rises to 10.96 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar cane crushing rises to 10.96 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai sugar cane crushing at all 46 mills rose to 10.96 million tonnes this season as of January 8 compared with 8.29 million tonnes on January 3, industry ministry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The mills produced 969,852 tonnes of sugar, 649,293 tonnes of which were raw and the rest refined, they told Reuters.</p>
<p>Thailand's crushing season normally starts in November and ends in May or June.</p>
<p>The yield rose to 88.48 kg of sugar per tonne of cane from 86.52 kg as of January 3.</p>
<p>Molasses production has so far reached 369,273 tonnes with a yield of 33.69 kg/tonne.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
